>  > - Restrict wand zapping to high-level monsters, especially the more
>  > deadly wands.  A Gnome Lord should be allowed to zap magic missiles.
> Death and sleep could be restricted, the others not.
> 
Actually what annoys me most, is that monsters have automatic identify.
Instead of artificial restrictions, give monster a chance of knowing
what the item is and how to use it (depending on its intelligence). Thus
a stupid troll usually wouldn't know how to use a wand of sleep - but
an elf lord almost always will... Would need to add another monster attribute
- intelligence (this can have interesting additional effect - more
intelligent monsters could e.g. recognise when you are stronger, and not 
try to attack you - until they find something like a wand of death or 
a named weapon...)

>  > - Make being killed when polymorphed lower your CON attribute, and if
>  > it is too low (< 5) you die for real.
> I never understood why you should revert to human when killed when polymorphed.
> You should simply die.
> 
That would add another 'arbitrary death' - player randomly polymorphed into
(say) a shrieker... As it is now he still has a chance. I can't understand 
why do you revert to human with full hit points through... Maybe you should 
come out weakened by the number of hp-s lost in another form (would mean, 
that you die if you get killed while polymorphed into something stronger 
than you).

